WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:17.775
"Mom and Dad are so lucky," Emmy said.

2
00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:21.295
"They took a trip to Spain!"

3
00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:24.153
Oliver frowned.

4
00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:27.982
"Why can't we take a trip?"

5
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:31.984
"We can have fun too," Aunt Judy said.

6
00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:36.105
"Let's go out to dinner."

7
00:00:36.106 --> 00:00:40.992
Aunt Judy brought everyone to a new restaurant.

8
00:00:40.993 --> 00:00:45.612
"They serve Korean food here," she said.

9
00:00:45.613 --> 00:00:50.137
Emmy sniffed.

10
00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:54.982
"It smells good!"

11
00:00:54.983 --> 00:01:00.780
A waiter brought menus.

12
00:01:00.781 --> 00:01:05.550
"They don't have grilled cheese," Oliver said.

13
00:01:05.551 --> 00:01:08.998
"No," Aunt Judy said.

14
00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:14.857
"But they have lots of interesting dishes."

15
00:01:14.858 --> 00:01:18.872
"They serve japchae," Harry said.

16
00:01:18.873 --> 00:01:20.863
"Those are noodles with vegetables.

17
00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:24.204
Yum."

18
00:01:24.205 --> 00:01:29.370
"Let's order a bunch of things," Aunt Judy said.

19
00:01:29.371 --> 00:01:34.417
Soon plates and bowls covered the table.

20
00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:38.553
Emmy tried a seafood pancake.

21
00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:43.320
"That's pajeon," Aunt Judy said.

22
00:01:43.321 --> 00:01:50.067
"Mmm," Emmy said. "Delicious!"

23
00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:54.475
Oliver looked at a bowl of bibimbap.

24
00:01:54.476 --> 00:01:58.330
"I like that dish," he said.

25
00:01:58.331 --> 00:02:04.522
"There's an egg on top!"

26
00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:10.124
The kids and Aunt Judy left the restaurant.

27
00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:12.988
Emmy's phone beeped.

28
00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:16.788
"Mom and Dad are calling," she said.

29
00:02:16.789 --> 00:02:20.913
"They want to chat with us."

30
00:02:20.914 --> 00:02:25.382
"Are you having a nice trip?" Oliver asked.

31
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:28.641
"Yes," Dad said.

32
00:02:28.642 --> 00:02:32.947
"Spain is beautiful!"

33
00:02:32.948 --> 00:02:36.395
"Where are you?" Mom asked.

34
00:02:36.396 --> 00:02:39.624
"I see a parking lot."

35
00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:45.946
Emmy laughed. "We took a trip too."

36
00:02:45.947 --> 00:02:51.479
Mom looked confused. "Where did you go?"

37
00:02:51.480 --> 00:03:00.546
Emmy grinned. "We went to Korea!"
